{"id": "8accf872-2b97-4ac3-aa68-65186ceec72d", "slug": "interplanetary-network-architecture", "title": "Interplanetary Network Architecture", "description": "Interplanetary Network Onboarding Section is designed for building reusable UI components in modern web projects. Key features include reusable structure, responsive behavior, and production-ready presentation. It is suitable for component libraries and responsive product interfaces.", "content": "---\nversion: \"neuform-staff-featured-2026-05-22\"\nname: \"Interplanetary Network Architecture\"\ndescription: \"Interplanetary Network Onboarding Section is designed for building reusable UI components in modern web projects. Key features include reusable structure, responsive behavior, and production-ready presentation. It is suitable for component libraries and responsive product interfaces.\"\ncolors:\n  primary: \"#38BDF8\"\n  secondary: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  accent: \"#60A5FA\"\n  background: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  surface: \"#A1A1AA\"\n  text-primary: \"#111827\"\n  text-secondary: \"#4B5563\"\n  border: \"#A1A1AA\"\ntypography:\n  display-lg:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"64px\"\n    fontWeight: 500\n    lineHeight: \"1.04\"\n    letterSpacing: \"0\"\n  body-md:\n    fontFamily: \"Quicksand\"\n    fontSize: \"16px\"\n    fontWeight: 400\n    lineHeight: \"1.6\"\n  label-md:\n    fontFamily: \"JetBrains Mono\"\n    fontSize: \"12px\"\n    fontWeight: 600\n    lineHeight: \"1.2\"\nspacing:\n  base: \"8px\"\n  gap: \"16px\"\n  card-padding: \"24px\"\n  section-padding: \"80px\"\nrounded:\n  card: \"8px\"\n  control: \"8px\"\n  pill: \"9999px\"\ncomponents:\n  card:\n    background: \"Use the surface token with subtle borders and HTML-matched shadow depth\"\n    radius: \"Match the declared card radius token\"\n  button:\n    background: \"Use primary or accent colors for the main action\"\n    radius: \"Use the control or pill radius based on the source HTML\"\n---\n# Interplanetary Network Architecture\nSource: Neuform staff featured templates. Author: Sourasith Phomhome (@madebysourasith). Views: 37; favorites: 3; remixes: 2.\nTags: onboarding, animated, webgl, threejs, charts, navigation, links, flow.\n## Overview\nInterplanetary Network Onboarding Section is designed for building reusable UI components in modern web projects. Key features include reusable structure, responsive behavior, and production-ready presentation. It is suitable for component libraries and responsive product interfaces.\n\nAether Architecture Protocols Telemetry Initialize Establishing the foundational topology for deep space high-bandwidth data transmission. LEO Relay Shell Lunar Relay Shell\n## Composition\nUse the attached HTML reference as the source of truth. Preserve the visible hierarchy, first-screen composition, section rhythm, density, and interaction tone before adapting copy or content.\nFollow the rendered preview for headline scale, supporting copy, navigation density, and component placement.\n## Colors\nAnchor the palette in primary #38BDF8, secondary #FFFFFF, accent #60A5FA, background #FFFFFF, surface #A1A1AA, text-primary #111827. Keep background, surface, text, and border roles distinct so generated layouts retain the same contrast pattern as the source.\n## Typography\nUse Inter for display moments and Quicksand for body copy unless the HTML clearly demands a compatible fallback. Labels and technical metadata should use JetBrains Mono or an equivalent mono face.\n## Layout\nKeep spacing deliberate and stable. Favor the same grid direction, max-width behavior, card density, and responsive stacking seen in the HTML. Do not replace distinctive source structures with generic SaaS sections.\n## Components\nDashboard, chart, and data panels should preserve their compact operational hierarchy, nested surfaces, and metric emphasis.\n## Motion\nPreserve existing motion cues such as masked reveals, staggered entrance, hover lift, scroll-triggered transitions, and ambient movement. Keep easing smooth and restrained.\n## WebGL & Effects\n\nIf the source includes canvas, WebGL, Three.js, gradients, particles, or atmospheric effects, rebuild them as supporting layers behind the content. Keep effects performant, responsive, and secondary to the interface.\n\n## Guardrails\n- Do not flatten the source into a generic card grid.\n- Do not swap the color mode unless the source clearly supports it.\n- Preserve the first viewport signal, focal object, and visual density.\n- Keep buttons, cards, and badges aligned to the same radius and border language.", "preview_html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\" class=\"bg-black\"><head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Interplanetary Network Architecture</title>\n    \n    <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://code.iconify.design/iconify-icon/1.0.7/iconify-icon.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/ScrollTrigger.min.js\"></script>\n    \n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin=\"\">\n    <link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&amp;display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n    \n    <style>\n        body {\n            font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;\n            background-color: #000000;\n        }\n        \n        .earth-texture {\n            background: radial-gradient(circle at 35% 35%, #e4e4e7 0%, #a1a1aa 20%, #3f3f46 60%, #09090b 100%);\n            box-shadow: inset -20px -20px 50px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9),\n                        inset 10px 10px 30px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n        }\n        \n        .moon-texture {\n            background: radial-gradient(circle at 40% 40%, #a1a1aa 0%, #52525b 40%, #18181b 85%, #000000 100%);\n            box-shadow: inset -10px -10px 25px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9),\n                        inset 5px 5px 15px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);\n        }\n\n        .map-overlay {\n            background-image: radial-gradient(#18181b 1px, transparent 1px);\n            background-size: 12px 12px;\n            opacity: 0.15;\n            mix-blend-mode: multiply;\n        }\n    </style>\n<link id=\"all-fonts-link-font-quicksand\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Quicksand:wght@300;400;500;600;700&amp;display=swap\"><style id=\"all-fonts-style-font-quicksand\">.font-quicksand { font-family: 'Quicksand', sans-serif !important; }</style></head>\n<body class=\"text-zinc-200 min-h-[150vh] overflow-x-hidden antialiased selection:bg-blue-500/30 flex flex-col\">\n\n    <!-- Subtle Navigation -->\n    <nav class=\"w-full px-8 py-6 flex items-center justify-between z-50 sticky top-0 bg-black/50 backdrop-blur-md border-b border-white/5\">\n        <div class=\"flex items-center gap-2 text-zinc-100 font-medium tracking-tight font-quicksand\">\n            <iconify-icon icon=\"solar:planet-4-linear\" class=\"text-xl\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></iconify-icon>\n            Aether\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"hidden md:flex items-center gap-8 text-sm font-medium text-zinc-400\">\n            <a href=\"#\" class=\"hover:text-white transition-colors font-quicksand\">Architecture</a>\n            <a href=\"#\" class=\"hover:text-white transition-colors font-quicksand\">Protocols</a>\n            <a href=\"#\" class=\"hover:text-white transition-colors font-quicksand\">Telemetry</a>\n        </div>\n        <button class=\"text-sm font-medium text-black bg-white px-4 py-2 rounded-full hover:bg-zinc-200 transition-colors font-quicksand\">\n            Initialize\n        </button>\n    </nav>\n\n    <main class=\"flex-grow flex flex-col items-center justify-start pt-24 md:pt-32 w-full relative z-10\">\n        \n        <!-- Masked Reveal Header -->\n        <div class=\"flex flex-col items-center w-full max-w-5xl px-6 mb-24 z-20\" id=\"hero-header\">\n            <h1 class=\"text-4xl md:text-6xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-center flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2\" id=\"masked-title\">\n                <!-- Word spans injected by JS -->\n            </h1>\n            <p class=\"mt-6 text-zinc-400 text-sm md:text-base max-w-2xl text-center opacity-0 font-quicksand\" id=\"subtitle\">\n                Establishing the foundational topology for deep space high-bandwidth data transmission.\n            </p>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Interactive Diagram Container -->\n        <div class=\"relative w-full max-w-[1200px] aspect-[1/1] md:aspect-[21/9] flex items-center justify-center mt-12 md:mt-0\" id=\"diagram-container\">\n            \n            <!-- Canvas for WebGL-style lines and particles -->\n            <canvas id=\"network-canvas\" class=\"absolute inset-0 w-full h-full z-0\"></canvas>\n\n            <!-- Earth Node (Left) -->\n            <div class=\"absolute left-1/2 md:left-[15%] top-[20%] md:top-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 md:-translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 flex flex-col items-center z-10\" id=\"earth-node\">\n                <!-- HTML Sphere -->\n                <div class=\"w-48 h-48 md:w-64 md:h-64 rounded-full earth-texture relative overflow-hidden flex items-center justify-center\">\n                    <div class=\"absolute inset-0 w-[200%] h-[200%] map-overlay rotate-12 scale-50\"></div>\n                </div>\n                \n                <!-- Label Line & Text -->\n                <div class=\"absolute top-full mt-6 md:mt-12 flex flex-col items-center\">\n                    <div class=\"w-px h-16 md:h-24 bg-zinc-700 mb-4 origin-top scale-y-0\" id=\"earth-line\"></div>\n                    <span class=\"text-xs md:text-sm text-zinc-400 font-medium tracking-wide whitespace-nowrap opacity-0 font-quicksand\" id=\"earth-label\">LEO Relay Shell</span>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <!-- Moon Node (Right) -->\n            <div class=\"absolute left-1/2 md:left-auto md:right-[15%] top-[80%] md:top-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 md:translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 flex flex-col items-center z-10\" id=\"moon-node\">\n                <!-- HTML Sphere -->\n                <div class=\"w-24 h-24 md:w-32 md:h-32 rounded-full moon-texture\"></div>\n                \n                <!-- Label Line & Text -->\n                <div class=\"absolute top-full mt-6 md:mt-12 flex flex-col items-center\">\n                    <div class=\"w-px h-16 md:h-24 bg-zinc-700 mb-4 origin-top scale-y-0\" id=\"moon-line\"></div>\n                    <span class=\"text-xs md:text-sm text-zinc-400 font-medium tracking-wide whitespace-nowrap opacity-0 font-quicksand\" id=\"moon-label\">Lunar Relay Shell</span>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <script>\n        // --- 1. GSAP Masked Reveal Setup ---\n        gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);\n\n        const titleText = \"Deploying the Interplanetary Network.\";\n        const titleContainer = document.getElementById('masked-title');\n        \n        // Wrap words for staggered reveal\n        titleText.split(' ').forEach(word => {\n            const wordSpan = document.createElement('span');\n            wordSpan.className = 'overflow-hidden inline-block py-1';\n            const innerSpan = document.createElement('span');\n            innerSpan.className = 'reveal-word inline-block translate-y-full';\n            innerSpan.innerText = word;\n            wordSpan.appendChild(innerSpan);\n            titleContainer.appendChild(wordSpan);\n        });\n\n        // Main Header Animation Timeline\n        const tl = gsap.timeline({\n            scrollTrigger: {\n                trigger: \"#hero-header\",\n                start: \"top 80%\",\n            }\n        });\n\n        tl.to(\".reveal-word\", {\n            y: 0,\n            stagger: 0.1,\n            duration: 1.2,\n            ease: \"power4.out\"\n        })\n        .to(\"#subtitle\", {\n            opacity: 1,\n            duration: 1,\n            ease: \"power2.out\"\n        }, \"-=0.6\")\n        // Diagram Labels Animation\n        .to([\"#earth-line\", \"#moon-line\"], {\n            scaleY: 1,\n            duration: 1,\n            ease: \"power3.inOut\"\n        }, \"-=0.5\")\n        .to([\"#earth-label\", \"#moon-label\"], {\n            opacity: 1,\n            y: -5,\n            duration: 0.8,\n            ease: \"power2.out\"\n        }, \"-=0.5\");\n\n\n        // --- 2. Advanced Canvas Networking Visualization ---\n        const canvas = document.getElementById('network-canvas');\n        const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\n        const container = document.getElementById('diagram-container');\n        const earthEl = document.getElementById('earth-node').firstElementChild;\n        const moonEl = document.getElementById('moon-node').firstElementChild;\n\n        let width, height;\n        let earthCenter = { x: 0, y: 0 };\n        let moonCenter = { x: 0, y: 0 };\n        let earthRadius = 0;\n        let moonRadius = 0;\n        let time = 0;\n\n        function resizeAndCalculate() {\n            width = container.offsetWidth;\n            height = container.offsetHeight;\n            \n            // Handle high-DPI displays\n            const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;\n            canvas.width = width * dpr;\n            canvas.height = height * dpr;\n            ctx.scale(dpr, dpr);\n            canvas.style.width = `${width}px`;\n            canvas.style.height = `${height}px`;\n\n            const containerRect = container.getBoundingClientRect();\n            const earthRect = earthEl.getBoundingClientRect();\n            const moonRect = moonEl.getBoundingClientRect();\n\n            // Calculate exact centers relative to canvas\n            earthCenter = {\n                x: (earthRect.left - containerRect.left) + earthRect.width / 2,\n                y: (earthRect.top - containerRect.top) + earthRect.height / 2\n            };\n            \n            moonCenter = {\n                x: (moonRect.left - containerRect.left) + moonRect.width / 2,\n                y: (moonRect.top - containerRect.top) + moonRect.height / 2\n            };\n\n            // Calculate shell radii (slightly larger than spheres)\n            const isMobile = window.innerWidth < 768;\n            const shellPadding = isMobile ? 16 : 28;\n            earthRadius = (earthRect.width / 2) + shellPadding;\n            moonRadius = (moonRect.width / 2) + (shellPadding * 0.8);\n        }\n\n        window.addEventListener('resize', resizeAndCalculate);\n        // Initial setup with a slight delay to ensure DOM is fully rendered\n        setTimeout(resizeAndCalculate, 100);\n\n        function drawShell(x, y, radius, dashOffset, dotCount) {\n            // Draw faint dashed ring\n            ctx.beginPath();\n            ctx.arc(x, y, radius, 0, Math.PI * 2);\n            ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2)';\n            ctx.lineWidth = 1;\n            ctx.setLineDash([2, 8]);\n            ctx.lineDashOffset = dashOffset;\n            ctx.stroke();\n\n            // Draw solid orbital dots\n            ctx.setLineDash([]);\n            for(let i = 0; i < dotCount; i++) {\n                const angle = (i / dotCount) * Math.PI * 2 + (dashOffset * -0.05);\n                const dotX = x + Math.cos(angle) * radius;\n                const dotY = y + Math.sin(angle) * radius;\n                \n                ctx.beginPath();\n                ctx.arc(dotX, dotY, 1.5, 0, Math.PI * 2);\n                ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9)';\n                ctx.fill();\n                \n                // Add a faint glow to dots\n                ctx.shadowColor = 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5)';\n                ctx.shadowBlur = 4;\n                ctx.fill();\n                ctx.shadowBlur = 0;\n            }\n        }\n\n        function drawNetworkLines() {\n            const numLines = 28;\n            const isVerticalLayout = Math.abs(earthCenter.x - moonCenter.x) < 50; // Simple mobile check\n\n            ctx.lineWidth = 1;\n\n            for (let i = 0; i < numLines; i++) {\n                const t = i / numLines;\n                \n                // Calculate angles around shells. The twist offset creates the complex criss-cross pattern\n                const angleEarth = t * Math.PI * 2;\n                const twist = Math.PI * 0.8;\n                const angleMoon = angleEarth + twist;\n\n                const startX = earthCenter.x + Math.cos(angleEarth) * earthRadius;\n                const startY = earthCenter.y + Math.sin(angleEarth) * earthRadius;\n\n                const endX = moonCenter.x + Math.cos(angleMoon) * moonRadius;\n                const endY = moonCenter.y + Math.sin(angleMoon) * moonRadius;\n\n                // Complex Bezier calculation for the \"pinched tube\" look\n                let cp1X, cp1Y, cp2X, cp2Y;\n                const pinchFactor = 0.5;\n\n                if (!isVerticalLayout) {\n                    // Desktop horizontal layout\n                    const midY = (earthCenter.y + moonCenter.y) / 2;\n                    cp1X = startX + (endX - startX) * 0.4;\n                    cp1Y = startY + (midY - startY) * pinchFactor;\n                    \n                    cp2X = endX - (endX - startX) * 0.4;\n                    cp2Y = endY + (midY - endY) * pinchFactor;\n                } else {\n                    // Mobile vertical layout\n                    const midX = (earthCenter.x + moonCenter.x) / 2;\n                    cp1X = startX + (midX - startX) * pinchFactor;\n                    cp1Y = startY + (endY - startY) * 0.4;\n                    \n                    cp2X = endX + (midX - endX) * pinchFactor;\n                    cp2Y = endY - (endY - startY) * 0.4;\n                }\n\n                ctx.beginPath();\n                ctx.moveTo(startX, startY);\n                ctx.bezierCurveTo(cp1X, cp1Y, cp2X, cp2Y, endX, endY);\n\n                // Styling the lines\n                // Fade out lines that go \"behind\" the spheres conceptually\n                const opacity = (Math.sin(angleEarth) > 0) ? 0.4 : 0.15;\n                ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(96, 165, 250, ${opacity})`; // Tailwind blue-400 equivalent\n                \n                // Animated data flow dashes\n                ctx.setLineDash([4, 18]);\n                ctx.lineDashOffset = -time * 25;\n                \n                // Add blue glow to connections\n                ctx.shadowColor = 'rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.4)';\n                ctx.shadowBlur = 6;\n                \n                ctx.stroke();\n                \n                // Reset shadow for next iteration\n                ctx.shadowBlur = 0;\n            }\n        }\n\n        function animate() {\n            // Clear canvas completely each frame\n            ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n\n            // Draw Earth Shell (counter-clockwise)\n            drawShell(earthCenter.x, earthCenter.y, earthRadius, time * 10, 36);\n            \n            // Draw Moon Shell (clockwise)\n            drawShell(moonCenter.x, moonCenter.y, moonRadius, -time * 15, 24);\n\n            // Draw Connections\n            drawNetworkLines();\n\n            time += 0.016; // approx 60fps\n            requestAnimationFrame(animate);\n        }\n\n        // Start animation loop once metrics are established\n        setTimeout(animate, 200);\n\n    </script>\n\n</body></html>", "preview_file_name": "interplanetary-network-architecture.html", "thumbnail_url": "https://hoirqrkdgbmvpwutwuwj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/design-system-thumbnails/staff-featured-2026-05-22/interplanetary-network-architecture.jpg", "source_name": "interplanetary-network-architecture-DESIGN.md", "views": 46, "forks": 4, "private": false, "featured": true, "created_by": "5bd6211c-bd4c-467c-b442-4312cac4712c", "created_at": "2026-06-12T07:38:10.793894+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-06-22T04:29:45.00689+00:00"}